.SH DESCRIPTION
Authenticates the client connection \f[CR]c\f[R] with the
\f[CR]bash\-server(1)\f[R] instance using the provided \f[CR]token\f[R].
This function must be called exactly once after establishing a
connection with \f[CR]bc_connect(3)\f[R] (or any other connection
function) and before issuing any commands.
.PP
The \f[CR]token\f[R] is a 64\-character hexadecimal string representing
a 256\-bit random value generated by the server at startup from
\f[CR]/dev/urandom\f[R].
The server performs constant\-time comparison to prevent timing attacks.
.PP
On the v2 protocol, authentication is sent as a JSON message on
\f[CR]CHAN_CONTROL\f[R] (channel 0) with type \f[CR]\(dqauth\(dq\f[R].
The server responds with either \f[CR]\(dqauth_ok\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(dqauth_fail\(dq\f[R].
.PP
If authentication fails, the connection remains open but in an
unauthenticated state.
The caller may retry with a different token or close the connection with
\f[CR]bc_close(3)\f[R].
