.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Authentication must be performed exactly once per connection.
Calling \f[CR]bc_auth\f[R] on an already\-authenticated connection
returns \f[CR]BC_ERR_PROTOCOL\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The token is compared using a constant\-time algorithm on the server
side to prevent timing\-based side\-channel attacks.
.IP \(bu 2
The 64\-character hex token represents 256 bits of entropy from
\f[CR]/dev/urandom\f[R].
Treat it as a secret \(en do not log it, embed it in source code, or
transmit it over insecure channels.
.IP \(bu 2
If the server was started with \f[CR]\-\-token <value>\f[R], use that
exact token.
Otherwise, read the auto\-generated token from the server\(cqs token
file (typically \f[CR]<socket_dir>/token\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
After a failed authentication attempt, the connection remains open.
The caller may retry with a different token.
However, the server may impose rate limits or close the connection after
repeated failures.
.IP \(bu 2
The function blocks until the server responds or the timeout expires.
The default timeout is 10 seconds.
